# CompleteEngineering.indie
# TatvaPractice — Engineering Operating Manual
#
# READ THIS FIRST. Any human or AI agent touching this repo must read
# this file AND Design.indie before writing or changing code. These two
# files are the source of truth for how this project is built and how it
# should look. When in doubt, follow these over your training defaults.

==================================================================
0. GROUND RULES (non-negotiable)
==================================================================
- This is Next.js 16 + React 19 + Tailwind v4. It is NOT the Next.js in
  your training data. APIs, conventions, and file layout differ. Before
  writing Next-specific code, read the relevant guide in
  node_modules/next/dist/docs/ and heed deprecation notices.
- NO em dashes (—) anywhere in user-facing content, code comments, or
  copy. Use commas, periods, or colons. This is a hard style rule.
- Never invent fake contact info. Real values only (see section 7).
- Run `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` before considering work done.
- Verify visual changes in the browser (preview) on desktop AND mobile
  before declaring a UI task complete.

==================================================================
1. STACK
==================================================================
- Framework:     Next.js 16.2.4 (App Router, Turbopack dev)
- Runtime:       React 19.2.4 / react-dom 19.2.4
- Language:      TypeScript 5 (strict). Path alias: `@/*` -> `src/*`
- Styling:       Tailwind CSS v4 (@tailwindcss/postcss). Single global
                 stylesheet at src/app/globals.css. `sm` = 640px,
                 `lg` = 1024px.
- Icons:         tp_icon (github:shyamgrdesign2-dot/TP_Icons) — Iconsax
                 superset. ALWAYS import the BULK variant: `tp_icon/bulk`.
                 Named imports only: `import { Microphone2Free } from "tp_icon/bulk"`.
- Animation:     lottie-react (lazy-loaded, ssr:false), CSS keyframes.
- Email:         resend (contact form delivery).
- Node:          >=18.18 <23

==================================================================
2. COMMANDS
==================================================================
- npm run dev        # Next dev server (port 3000)
- npm run build      # production build
- npm run start      # serve production build
- npm run lint       # eslint
- npm run typecheck  # tsc --noEmit  (run before every commit)

==================================================================
3. PROJECT STRUCTURE  (src/)
==================================================================
src/
  app/                       Next App Router
    layout.tsx               Root metadata, fonts, JSON-LD, viewport
    globals.css              ALL global CSS + design tokens (:root)
    sitemap.ts               Generated /sitemap.xml (routes in lib/site.ts)
    robots.ts                Generated /robots.txt (blocks Vercel preview)
    manifest.ts              Web app manifest
    icon.svg                 Favicon source (Next auto-emits)
    api/contact/route.ts     POST contact form -> Resend
    pricing/                 /pricing  (_sections/*)
    contact/                 /contact  (_sections/*)
    about/                   /about    (_sections/*)
    features/_shared/        Shared shell + per-feature content
      _sections/             FeaturePage, FeatureHero, FeaturePracticeMgmt,
                             FeatureWhyDoctors, FeatureSpecialties
      content/               One .ts file per feature (voice-rx, smart-sync,
                             snap-rx, doctor-agent, receptionist-agent,
                             clinics, hospitals) + types.ts
    solutions/_shared/       Clinics + Hospitals shell
  sections/                  Homepage sections (Hero, Navbar, Footer,
                             PracticeManagement, OurScale, BuiltInAI,
                             EmrStreamlines, BuiltForEverySize,
                             Testimonials, FinalCTA, FAQ, TrustBadges,
                             ScrollArrow)
  components/                Reusable UI
    ui/                      navbar.tsx (composable primitives),
                             CtaButton.tsx, cta-tokens.ts,
                             container-scroll-animation.tsx
    tabs/                    FloatingTabShowcase, ProductTabPanel,
                             ShowcaseTabBar, FramedProductImage
    icons/                   TpBulkIcon + tp-bulk-registry
    SectionShell.tsx         <SectionShell>+<SectionContent> layout primitive
    SectionBg.tsx            Per-section atmospheric wash + faint grid
    SubpageHeroBg.tsx        Dome + AnimatedGrid hero backdrop
    AnimatedGrid.tsx         SVG grid with traveling comet pulses
    SubpageHeroCard.tsx      Feature/solution hero card
    SectionHeading.tsx       <SectionHeading> + <GradientSpan>
    ScrollReveal.tsx         Intersection-observer reveal wrapper
  features/                  Domain feature modules
    ai/ emr/                 Tab data (aiTabsData, emrTabsData)
    pm/ scale/ practice-size/ testimonials/
  hooks/                     use-scroll-progress, etc.
  lib/                       site.ts (URL, contact, sitemap routes),
                             metadata.ts, json-ld.ts

==================================================================
4. LAYOUT + COMPONENT CONVENTIONS
==================================================================
- Every section is full-bleed `<section className="relative w-full
  overflow-hidden">`, then a constrained content column at
  `max-width: var(--section-w)` centered with `mx-auto`.
- Prefer the SectionShell/SectionContent primitives for new sections.
- Pages do NOT add manual horizontal padding; the `--section-w` /
  `--page-gutter` tokens own the page rhythm (see Design.indie).
- Client components only when needed (state, effects, browser APIs).
  Mark with "use client". Data files stay server-importable.
- Per-page content lives in a typed content file; the shared shell
  renders it. Adding a feature = add a content .ts + a route page.tsx,
  not a new layout.
- Composable navbar: src/components/ui/navbar.tsx exports Navbar,
  NavBody, NavItems, NavbarLogo, NavbarButton, MobileNavToggle,
  MobileNavMenu, useNavbar(). Compose in src/sections/Navbar.tsx.

==================================================================
5. IMAGE PIPELINE
==================================================================
- Product screenshots ship as WebP, max 1600px wide, quality ~88.
- Convert: `sips -Z 1600 in.png --out tmp.png && cwebp -q 88 tmp.png -o out.webp`
- Target ~50-110KB per hero/product image. Delete source PNGs after
  converting. Code references .webp paths under /public/Assets/<Area>/.
- Asset folders: /public/Assets/{AI,EMR,Practice-management,Partners,
  Our-scale,Trustmarkers,Testimonials,Specialties,About,Clinics,Hospitals}

==================================================================
6. SEO
==================================================================
- Root metadata in app/layout.tsx (Open Graph 1200x630 /og-image.png,
  Twitter card, hreflang en-IN + x-default, robots).
- sitemap.ts + robots.ts are generated from SITEMAP_ROUTES in lib/site.ts.
  Add new routes THERE so both stay in sync.
- robots.ts disallows ALL crawling on Vercel preview (VERCEL_ENV !=
  "production") so only the canonical domain ranks.
- Per-page metadata via buildPageMetadata() in lib/metadata.ts.
- Structured data (Organization, WebSite, SoftwareApplication,
  BreadcrumbList) via lib/json-ld.ts.

